=======================================================

FIXFLOW IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE
Simple Hinglish version

IS DOCUMENT KA PURPOSE
Ye coding nahi hai. Ye ek task-by-task plan hai jo batata hai ki FixFlow backend banate waqt pehle kya karna hai, uske baad kya, kaun si files badalengi, aur task complete kaise verify hoga.

KAISE USE KARNA HAI
Ek waqt par sirf ek task uthao. Uske prerequisites pehle complete hone chahiye. Task khud implement karne ki koshish karo; jahan atko, AI agent se sirf usi task par help lo. Code review aur tests pass hone ke baad hi status Completed karo.

STATUS KA MATLAB
Not Started = abhi shuru nahi hua. In Progress = kaam chal raha hai. Blocked = kisi decision ya dependency ki wajah se rukha hai. Completed = implementation aur verification sach mein ho chuki hai.

PROJECT KI CURRENT POSITION
Checklist ke mutabik basic Express server, health endpoint aur 404/error handling setup ho chuka bataya gaya hai. MongoDB connection, models, authentication, repair APIs, automated tests, API documentation aur deployment abhi baaki hain. Repository/Git initialization bhi checklist ke mutabik unchecked hai. Apne actual files aur test output se status confirm karna.

PHASE 0 — Initial setup
-----------------------

SETUP-01 — Basic backend setup
Maqsad: Express server chalna chahiye aur local secrets Git mein upload nahi hone chahiye.
Kaam: package scripts/dependencies, app.js aur server.js ka separation, dotenv, GET /health, JSON parsing, 404/error response, .gitignore aur .env.example verify karo. Is task mein MongoDB connect nahi karna.
Test: npm run dev chalao; /health par 200 JSON aur unknown route par 404 JSON check karo; server band karo; confirm karo .env aur node_modules ignored hain.
Status in checklist: Completed (reported; actual repo mein dobara verify karna).

PHASE 1 — Shared infrastructure and testing foundation
------------------------------------------------------

DB-01 — Database configuration decide karna
Maqsad: MongoDB connection string environment variable ka naam aur missing configuration par server ka behavior decide karna.
Kaam: .env.example mein sirf placeholder rakho; real credentials sirf local ignored .env mein. Provider choose karna is task ka part nahi.
Test: .env aur .env.example check karo; tracked file mein real secret na ho.
Status: Not Started. Decision chahiye: variable ka exact naam aur invalid/missing value par behavior.

DB-02 — MongoDB connect karna
Maqsad: Database connect hone ke baad hi server requests serve kare.
Kaam: Mongoose connection code, environment validation, startup failure logging aur clean shutdown. Abhi models ya business logic mat banao.
Test: valid database par start karo; missing config aur unreachable database par startup fail hota hai ya nahi check karo; shutdown clean hona chahiye.
Status: Not Started. Decision chahiye: /health sirf server alive batayega ya database readiness bhi.

ERR-01 — Standard error response
Maqsad: API errors har jagah consistent hon aur internal details/stack trace user ko na mile.
Kaam: centralized error handler ko API contract ke response format ke saath align karo; validation, auth, permission, not-found, conflict aur unexpected errors ke status decide karo.
Test: unknown route, malformed JSON aur unexpected error test karo; response mein stack trace/secrets nahi hone chahiye.
Status: Not Started. Decision chahiye: error JSON ka final format aur validation ke liye HTTP 400 ya 422.

VAL-01 — Request validation
Maqsad: Galat input business logic ya database tak pahunchne se pehle reject ho.
Kaam: validation library/approach select karo; request body aur route params validate karo; protected fields ko accept mat karo.
Test: invalid input reject ho; valid input hi controller/service tak pahuche.
Status: Not Started. Decision chahiye: kaunsi validation library/schema style use hogi.

TEST-01 — Automated testing setup
Maqsad: Har feature ko repeatable tests se verify karna, sirf manually check nahi karna.
Kaam: test runner select karo, npm test command set karo aur safe test database strategy decide karo. Production database ko tests mein use mat karna.
Test: ek test command successfully run ho aur failure hone par non-zero exit code de.
Status: Not Started. Decision chahiye: test runner aur integration-test database approach.

PHASE 2 — Users and authentication
----------------------------------

USER-01 — User model
Maqsad: User ka naam, email, password hash, role aur active status database mein safely store karna.
Kaam: Mongoose schema, timestamps, normalized/unique email, role enum aur password hash ko normal response se hide karna.
Test: invalid role/required fields reject hon; duplicate email handle ho; password hash normal response mein na aaye.
Status: Not Started.

AUTH-01 — Customer registration
Maqsad: Customer apna account create kar sake.
Kaam: POST /api/v1/auth/register, input validation, email normalization, password hashing, safe response aur duplicate email handling.
Security: public user kabhi request body mein role=admin/technician bhej kar privileged account create na kar sake; backend role customer set kare.
Test: valid registration, duplicate email, invalid input aur role-escalation attempts test karo. Status: Not Started.

AUTH-02 — Login and access token
Maqsad: Registered user credentials verify karke access token issue karna.
Kaam: POST /api/v1/auth/login, password hash compare, inactive account reject aur safe token response.
Test: correct password, wrong password, unknown email aur inactive account. Error response se ye leak nahi hona chahiye ki email registered hai ya nahi.
Status: Not Started. Decision chahiye: access-token expiry, signing method/library, secret/key config aur token claims.

AUTH-03 — Authenticate requests / current user
Maqsad: Token verify karke pata lagana ki request kis user ki hai.
Kaam: authentication middleware aur GET /api/v1/auth/me. Missing/invalid/expired token ko reject karo; safe profile return karo.
Test: valid, missing, malformed, expired aur invalid token ke cases.
Status: Not Started.

AUTH-04 — Role authorization
Maqsad: Customer, technician aur admin sirf allowed actions kar saken.
Kaam: reusable authorization middleware; unauthenticated user ke liye 401, logged-in but unauthorized role ke liye 403.
Test: har role ke allowed aur blocked endpoints verify karo. Client-side checks ko security ka replacement mat samjho.
Status: Not Started.

SESS-01 — Refresh session model
Maqsad: Refresh sessions ko revoke/expire kar pana, raw refresh token database mein save kiye bina.
Kaam: session model, user reference, tokenHash, expiry/revocation fields aur TTL cleanup index; application ko expiry khud bhi verify karni hogi.
Test: stored value hash ho, raw token nahi; expiry aur revocation ka behavior verify karo.
Status: Not Started. Decision chahiye: refresh lifetime, rotation, reuse detection aur concurrent-session policy.

SESS-02 — Refresh token endpoint
Maqsad: Valid refresh credential se naya access token aur policy ke mutabik naya refresh token issue karna.
Kaam: POST /api/v1/auth/refresh; expiry/revocation/rotation/reuse policy implement karo.
Test: valid refresh, expired/revoked token, old token reuse aur concurrency policy.
Status: Not Started; SESS-01 ke decisions par depend karta hai.

SESS-03 — Logout
Maqsad: Logout par sahi refresh session revoke ho.
Kaam: POST /api/v1/auth/logout; user kisi aur ka session revoke na kar sake.
Test: logout ke baad refresh fail ho; doosre user ka session revoke karne ki koshish reject ho.
Status: Not Started. Decision chahiye: sirf current session logout hoga ya all sessions.

PHASE 3 — Repair model and basic APIs
-------------------------------------

REP-01 — Repair lifecycle decisions
Maqsad: Repair request ke statuses aur estimate approval/rejection ka ek clear design banana.
Kaam: decide karo APPROVED/REJECTED repair status honge ya estimate response metadata; cancellation allowed states; rejected estimate revise ho sakta hai ya request close hogi; admin override/audit rules.
Test: har actor action aur status transition ko ek consistent table mein review karo; runtime code abhi nahi.
Status: Not Started. Ye decisions repair schema banane se pehle resolve karo.

REP-02 — Repair model and transition logic
Maqsad: Repair request database mein save ho aur status sirf allowed sequence mein change ho.
Kaam: customer/technician references, device details, status, estimate, status history aur timestamps; service-level transition rules.
Test: invalid status/transition reject ho; status change aur history match karein; references valid hon.
Status: Not Started. Device types aur text field limits decide karni hain.

REP-03 — Customer repair request create kare
Maqsad: Logged-in customer repair request submit kar sake.
Kaam: POST /api/v1/repairs; customer ID authenticated user se lo; initial status backend set kare.
Security: client ke customerId, technicianId ya status par trust mat karo.
Test: request create karo; forged IDs/status bhejo; saved owner aur status verify karo. Status: Not Started.

REP-04 — Repairs list/read with access control
Maqsad: Har user sirf wahi repairs dekh sake jinke liye woh authorized hai.
Kaam: GET /api/v1/repairs aur GET /api/v1/repairs/:id. Customer ko apne, technician ko assigned, admin ko authorized records dikhein.
Test: multiple users/roles ke records ke saath list/detail endpoints aur unauthorized IDs test karo.
Status: Not Started. Decision chahiye: pagination format aur hidden resource ke liye 404 vs 403 policy.

PHASE 4 — Assignment and repair workflow
----------------------------------------

TECH-01 — Technician account provisioning
Maqsad: Assignment ke liye eligible technician account create/activate karne ka safe process define karna.
Kaam: decide karo admin directly account create karega ya invitation flow hoga. Public registration customer-only rahe.
Test: customer/technician ko unauthorized technician provisioning na karne do.
Status: Not Started. Decision chahiye: admin-created accounts vs invitations.

REP-05 — Admin technician assign kare
Maqsad: Admin repair request ko active technician ko assign kar sake.
Kaam: POST /api/v1/repairs/:id/assign; target user technician role aur active hona chahiye; allowed state mein hi assign ho; history record ho.
Test: valid assignment, wrong role/inactive technician, non-admin caller aur invalid repair state.
Status: Not Started.

REP-06 — Technician estimate submit kare
Maqsad: Assigned technician repair cost estimate submit kar sake.
Kaam: POST /api/v1/repairs/:id/estimate; amount, INR currency aur notes validate karo; client status set na kar sake.
Test: assigned vs other technician, invalid amount, wrong state aur repeated/revision attempts.
Status: Not Started. Decision chahiye: rejected estimate revise ho sakta hai ya nahi, aur field limits.

REP-07 — Customer estimate approve/reject kare
Maqsad: Sirf repair ka owner pending estimate par decision de.
Kaam: POST /api/v1/repairs/:id/estimate-response; approve/reject choice validate; owner aur pending-state enforce; status/history consistent rakho.
Test: owner, non-owner, wrong role, duplicate response aur estimate se pehle response.
Status: Not Started.

REP-08 — Customer cancellation
Maqsad: Customer sirf allowed pre-work state mein apni request cancel kar sake.
Kaam: POST /api/v1/repairs/:id/cancel; ownership aur approved cancellation policy enforce; history record karo.
Test: allowed aur disallowed states, owner/non-owner, in-progress/completed cancellation.
Status: Not Started. Decision chahiye: assignment ke baad cancellation aur admin override.

REP-09 — Technician repair start kare
Maqsad: Assigned technician sirf approved repair start kar sake.
Kaam: POST /api/v1/repairs/:id/start; only approved state se IN_PROGRESS; history record ho.
Test: correct technician and approved state; unapproved, cancelled, completed ya different technician cases reject hon.
Status: Not Started.

REP-10 — Technician repair complete kare
Maqsad: Assigned technician in-progress repair ko complete kar sake.
Kaam: POST /api/v1/repairs/:id/complete; only IN_PROGRESS -> COMPLETED; history update ho.
Test: before-start completion, repeated completion aur wrong technician reject hon.
Scope: payment/notifications/delivery jaise unrequested features add mat karo. Status: Not Started.

PHASE 5 — Security, tests, documentation, deployment
----------------------------------------------------

SEC-01 — Security review
Maqsad: Deployment se pehle saare implemented endpoints ka security audit.
Check: customer-only registration, password hashing, hashed refresh tokens, role/ownership checks, protected fields, input validation, status transitions, secret/hash/stack-trace leakage, session expiry/revocation, query scoping aur npm audit findings.
Test: cross-user access, role escalation, token misuse aur error leakage ke regression tests.
Status: Not Started.

TEST-02 — Full API/lifecycle tests
Maqsad: End-to-end confirm karna ki documented flow aur error behavior sahi hai.
Kaam: auth, sessions, roles, ownership, validation, duplicate/conflict actions aur har allowed repair transition test karo. Test data isolated ho; production services use na hon.
Test: single documented command se test suite run ho; Postman mein register/login se repair complete/cancel tak flow test karo.
Status: Not Started.

DOC-01 — API documentation
Maqsad: Developers API ko documentation follow karke use kar saken.
Kaam: actual methods/paths, auth, roles, request/response examples, status codes, error shape, pagination aur state rules document karo.
Test: examples ko actual API responses se compare karo; planned behavior ko implemented behavior ke roop mein mat likho.
Status: Not Started. Decisions chahiye: pagination, error response policy aur Postman collection chahiye ya nahi.

DEPLOY-01 — Hosting target choose karna
Maqsad: Decide karna ki backend kahan deploy hoga.
Kaam: ek platform choose karke Node version, env vars, database connectivity aur start command document karo.
Test: selected platform ke saath project compatibility review karo.
Status: Not Started. Hosting platform abhi selected nahi.

DEPLOY-02 — Deploy and verify
Maqsad: Backend ko selected platform par deploy karke real health/API smoke test pass karna.
Kaam: runtime/start command/secrets configure karo; intended database connect karo; startup/shutdown logs review karo; credentials source/build artifacts mein na hon.
Test: deployed /health aur safe API flow verify karo; tests deployment se pehle pass hone chahiye.
Status: Not Started.

IMPORTANT OPEN DECISIONS
-------------------------

- Repair states: APPROVED/REJECTED ko repair status mein rakhna hai ya estimate response metadata mein? Duplicate information avoid karni hai.
- Cancellation: Assignment ke baad aur estimate se pehle cancellation allowed hogi? Admin override/audit ka rule kya hoga?
- Rejected estimate: Reject hone par request close hogi ya technician revised estimate de sakta hai?
- Field limits: Device type values aur issue description/device fields ki maximum length kya hogi?
- Technician accounts: Admin directly account banayega/activate karega ya invitation system hoga?
- Tokens/sessions: Access/refresh expiry, token rotation, reuse detection, logout scope aur concurrent sessions ka rule kya hai?
- Error format: API errors ka final JSON envelope kya hoga? Validation ke liye 400 ya 422?
- Testing/validation tools: Kaunsa validation tool aur test runner/database strategy use karni hai?
- Pagination/deployment: List APIs ka pagination format aur deployment platform kya hoga?

RULE: Ek task at a time. Prerequisites complete karo, implementation review karo, tests run karo, phir status update karo. AI agent ka 'done' kehna akela proof nahi hai.